  "live_records": {
    "q-213136": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213136",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $6x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,35)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nThe modulus equals $35$ in all statements, which suggests we'll need to use the first property.\n\nNotice that the coefficient of $x$ is $6,$ and $6\\cdot 6=36$ is one larger than the modulus. Therefore, we can reduce the coefficient of $x$ to unity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\ 6\\cdot 6x & ≡6\\cdot 1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\ 36x & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\ x+35x & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\ x+0x & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,35) \\\\ x & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,35)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
