    "q-213139": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213139",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $7x≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,20)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nThe modulus equals $20$ in all statements, which suggests we'll need to use the first property.\n\nNotice that the coefficient of $x$ is $7,$ and $3\\cdot 7=21$ is one larger than the modulus. Therefore, we can reduce the coefficient of $x$ to unity as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,20) \\\\ 3\\cdot 7x & ≡3\\cdot 1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,20) \\\\ 21x & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,20) \\\\ x+20x & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,20) \\\\ x+0x & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,20) \\\\ x & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,20)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
