    "q-213125": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213125",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $w≡z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15),$ construct a statement that also must be true:\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}w≡{{field-2}}z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The scalar multiplication properties of congruences state that for $k\\in Z,$ we have the following:\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- $a≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟹\\,ka≡kb\\,(\\text{mod}\\,kn)$\n\nSince the modulus is unchanged in both statements, let's multiply by $4$ and apply the first property.\n\n$$\nw≡z\\,⟹\\,4w≡4z\\,(\\text{mod}\\,15)\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
