    "q-213040": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213040",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "By the multiplicative property of congruences, $77\\cdot 82≡$",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}77 & ≡12\\cdot 6+5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡12\\cdot 0+5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\ 82 & ≡13\\cdot 6+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡13\\cdot 0+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}77\\cdot 82 & ≡5\\cdot 4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡20\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡3\\cdot 6+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡3\\cdot 0+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6) \\\\  & ≡2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n77\\cdot 82≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,6).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
