    "q-213207": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213207",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Use the multiplicative property of congruences to compute the following residue.\n\n$124\\cdot 99\\text{ mod }5=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}124 & ≡24\\cdot 5+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡24\\cdot 0+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\ 99 & ≡19\\cdot 5+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡19\\cdot 0+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}124\\cdot 99 & ≡4\\cdot 4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡16\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3\\cdot 5+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3\\cdot 0+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡0+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n124\\cdot 99\\text{ mod }5=1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
