    "q-213012": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213012",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "By the multiplicative property of congruences, $73\\cdot 88≡$",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}73 & ≡14\\cdot 5+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡14\\cdot 0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\ 88 & ≡17\\cdot 5+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡17\\cdot 0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}73\\cdot 88 & ≡3\\cdot 3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡9\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡5+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡0+4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡4\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n73\\cdot 88≡4\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
