    "q-213038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213038",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "By the multiplicative property of congruences, $95\\cdot 109≡$",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}95 & ≡11\\cdot 8+7\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡11\\cdot 0+7\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡7\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\ 109 & ≡13\\cdot 8+5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡13\\cdot 0+5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}95\\cdot 109 & ≡7\\cdot 5\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡35\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡4\\cdot 8+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡4\\cdot 0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n95\\cdot 109≡3\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213038-a",
