    "q-213033": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213033",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "By the multiplicative property of congruences, $92\\cdot 93≡$",
      "worked_solution": "The multiplicative property of modular congruences states that if\n\n$$\na≡b\\,\\text{and}\\,c≡d\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n),\n$$\n\nthen, we have \n\n$$\nac≡bd\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}92 & ≡18\\cdot 5+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡18\\cdot 0+2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡2\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\ 93 & ≡18\\cdot 5+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡18\\cdot 0+3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the multiplicative property of congruences, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}92\\cdot 93 & ≡2\\cdot 3\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡6\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡5+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡0+1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5) \\\\  & ≡1\\, & (\\text{mod}\\,5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n92\\cdot 93≡1\\,(\\text{mod}\\,5).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
